TYPES.md §15: a user method called in a field default, bare or through `self`, is a user function: E3010 other, once each at the call.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record R {
  a: Int = 1
  b: Int = self.twice()
  c: Int = twice()

  fn twice(self) -> Int { return a * 2 }
}
